   "line": [
    "Nxe4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A tactic to watch for in the resulting position — a knight leap to f5 becomes possible precisely because the central pawn hasn't moved yet, so that square isn't yet under control. Always check which squares your own un-played pawns are leaving open.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 399,
   "fen": "rnbqr1k1/pppp1p2/7p/2b2Np1/4n3/2N3B1/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R b KQ - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "Nf5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Don't snatch the bishop — the recapture would open a file and hand the opponent pressure. Instead the knight captures on c3, and the in-between check doesn't work because the king simply steps up and wins the piece back. Calculate the zwischenzug one step further before trusting it.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 476,
   "fen": "rnbqr1k1/pppp1p2/7p/2b2Np1/8/2n3B1/PPP1BPPP/R2QK2R w KQ - 0 11",
