   "spoken": "And a trap in that line to avoid: the popular wrong answer thinks it wins a rook, but calculating one move further, a queen move gathers two pieces for the rook and full compensation — so a quieter queen retreat is the safer route, only switching back to winning the rook once the knight can't be given for it. Don't stop calculating at the move that looks like it wins.",
