   "spoken": "The deeper lesson of the whole game — there's a clear shift as you improve. Early on, chess is applying the rules by the book, and it wins plenty of games. To go further you must know the rules cold and also know when to break them: this is underdeveloped, this weakens my king, yet the specific features of the position let me get away with it. That's where concrete calculation transcends general reasoning.",
